Project Introduction
Name: Praveen
Role: Automation Tester Intern
Organization: Cubera Tech

Overview 
During my internship at Cubera Tech, I had the opportunity to design and develop an Automation Testing Framework using Cypress, integrated with BDD (Cucumber) and the Page Object Model (POM) design pattern. The main objective of this project was to create a scalable, maintainable, and readable test automation framework that ensures reliable end-to-end testing of web applications.

Project Description
This project represents the outcome of my learning and hands-on exploration of modern test automation practices using Cypress.
I explored and implemented:
•	Behaviour-Driven Development (BDD) principles to write human-readable test cases.
•	Page Object Model (POM) for structured and reusable code.
•	Cypress commands and hooks for efficient test execution.
•	Test data management using JSON files.
•	Moch awesome reporting for detailed visual reports.

Outcome
By the end of this project, I successfully built a complete Cypress Automation Framework capable of:
•	Handling multiple modules and test scenarios.
•	Providing clear and descriptive reports.
•	Supporting continuous integration in real-world testing environments

Project Dependencies and Purpose:
1.	Cypress: npm install cypress --save-dev
Purpose: The core testing framework used for end-to-end web automation. Provides commands like cy. visit (), cy.get (), and integrates with browsers for UI testing

3.	@badeball/cypress-cucumber-preprocessor:
   npm install @badeball/cypress-cucumber-preprocessor --save-dev
   Purpose: Enables BDD (Cucumber) support in Cypress — allows writing test  
    cases in Gherkin syntax (.feature files).
  	
4.	@cucumber/gherkin: npm install @cucumber/gherkin --save-dev
    Purpose: Parses and executes Gherkin syntax used in feature files (Given, When, Then statements).

5.	@cypress/webpack-preprocessor : 
    npm install @cypress/webpack-preprocessor --save-dev    
    Purpose: Required by the Cucumber preprocessor to compile .feature files and step definitions before running them.

5.	@bahmutov/cypress-esbuild-preprocessor :
    npm install @bahmutov/cypress-esbuild-preprocessor --save-dev
    Purpose: A faster alternative to webpack for compiling feature files; used in modern setups for performance.


